  "rationale": "The iterative and unrolled_k families are fundamentally incapable of meeting the throughput constraint. The best throughput observed was 8.68 MSPS (iterative), which is less than 1/5th of the required 50 MSPS. Since these architectures produce one result every N+3 or ceil(N/k)+3 cycles respectively, their throughput is inherently limited by the number of iterations required for accuracy (N >= 14-15 to meet the error constraint). To achieve 50 MSPS, we need an architecture that produces one result per cycle. The 'pipelined' and 'pipelined_m' families are the only ones in the registry that offer 1 result/cycle throughput. Therefore, we must explore these families to find a feasible design.",
